[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 1"""
 date="2026-11-17T15:31:57Z"
 content="""
Maybe another angle on this is that git-annex branch changes with
incorrect information for the local repository should be automatically
corrected.

Then the existing repository size tracking could be used for a quota
(Ignoring keys w/o a stated size which could just be rejected from
being received by a repository with a quota). Perhaps supplimented
with the size of partially transferred objects.

Since calcBranchRepoSizes already sees all changes to location logs,
it could just check if changes for the local repository are accurate.
And journal a correction to the location log when they're not.

When the git-annex branch is updated locally, we know those changes are
accurate, so it could skip the double checking them. That would make
this have almost zero overhead.
"""]]
